course: dictionary
lesson: 8993
title: Sixty, six tens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sixty is a number. It is the number 60, which is six tens. You can write it with digits as 60, or say the word sixty.
explain: Sixty is a helpful number for telling time. «60 seconds make a minute and 60 minutes make an hour», so when a time problem mentions sixty, think about the clock.
explain: Context shows you what sixty is counting. «Its emperors Kangxi and Qianlong ruled about sixty years each» means years, and «sixty miles an hour» is a speed. Ask yourself: what is being counted?
fact: Sixty means 60, which is six tens.
fact: There are 60 seconds in a minute and 60 minutes in an hour.
fact: The Sumerians counted in groups of sixty, which is why we still use 60 seconds in a minute.
fact: A second is about as long as saying «one Mississippi» at a calm speed.
fact: «Sixty» can count years, as in «ruled about sixty years» for Emperor Kangxi and Emperor Qianlong.
exercise: How many minutes are in one hour? | 30 | *60 | 6 | 100
exercise: Sixty is the same as how many tens? | 0 tens | *6 tens | 60 tens | 16 tens
exercise: How many seconds are in one minute? | *60 | 6 | 600 | 16
test: «The Sumerians counted in groups of sixty.» Which number is sixty written with digits? | 6 | *60 | 600 | 16
test: A road sign says «sixty miles an hour». What does sixty tell you? | *The speed limit | The number of minutes in a day | Sixteen miles an hour | Six miles an hour
exam: How many seconds are in 2 minutes? | *120 | 60 | 100 | 12
